\section{Introduction}
Tigrigna (Tigrinya, ISO 639-3: tir) is a Semitic language of Eritrea and Tigray, Ethiopia, written in the Ge'ez script. It is used as a language of instruction. My searches were in English and found no official Ministry of Education textbooks; the findings below are mostly diaspora and learner materials, and searching in Ge'ez script would likely turn up more.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Press release on Weledo's Tigrinya grammar book for diaspora children (sentence structure, spelling, verb agreement, phonology): \url{https://www.newswire.com/news/weledos-latest-tigrinya-book-expected-to-impact-how-tigrinya-mother-31201}
\item Same announcement, alternate link: \url{https://www.newswire.com/weledo-s-latest-tigrinya-book-expected/220072}
\item Tigrinya for Beginners (Ge'ez script learner book): \url{https://betterread.com.au/book/tigrinya-for-beginners.do}
\item Basic Tigrinya (audiobook listing): \url{https://www.audiobooksnow.com/audiobook/basic-tigrinya/10319184/}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Cambridge Language Centre, The essential guide to Tigrinya: \url{https://www.langcen.cam.ac.uk/resources/langt/data/tr_103.html}
\item Cambridge Language Centre, Tigrinya grammar: \url{https://www.langcen.cam.ac.uk/resources/langt/data/tr_104.html}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found in search results.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Goethe-Verlag, Learn Tigrinya online: \url{https://www.goethe-verlag.com/learn-tigrinya-online.html}
